Per user direction 2026-05-19 (AskUserQuestion answer post-PR-status-check):
"Dispatch confirmatory spike before closure" for PR #585's NEW POSITIVE
CMB R4-1 chain p=0.04 hidden-fiber correlation claim.

Verdict: H0-NOT-REPRODUCED. The marginal positive does not reproduce
under any of the standard rigor tests.

Multi-seed replication of PR #585's exact null test:
- 10 random seeds, 50 uniform eigs in [0,250], 10000 trials each
- p range: 0.0518 - 0.0584 (mean 0.0552)
- PR #585's reported p=0.041 is BELOW ALL 10 replications
- Likely an undocumented outlier seed

Independent-dataset replication:
- Planck PR3 (Aghanim+ 2020 arXiv:1807.06209): p=0.19
- WMAP 9yr (Hinshaw+ 2013 arXiv:1212.5226): p=1.00
- ACT DR4 (Aiola+ 2020 arXiv:2007.07288): p=0.14
- SPT-3G (Dutcher+ 2021 arXiv:2101.01684): p=0.87
- Planck PR4 (Akrami+ 2020 arXiv:2007.04997): p=0.19
- No independent dataset reaches p<0.05

Bonferroni correction:
- 5-6 tests in Spike #47 R4-1 + PR #585 cluster
- Bonferroni-corrected alpha: 0.010 - 0.0083
- Even replicated p~=0.055 fails nominal alpha=0.05
- Independent best p=0.14 fails Bonferroni by an order of magnitude

Researcher-degrees-of-freedom problem:
- 23,760 valid integer chains match Planck peaks within 1.6% tolerance
- PR #585's chain ranks 745/23,760 (top 3.1 percentile)
- Chain biased toward squashed-S^7 eigenvalues
- Chain entry Lambda=28 violates stated tolerance (1.63% vs 1.6% max)
- Best-Planck-faithful chain {2,12,27,52,83,127,174,228}: p=0.171

Structural diagnosis: squashed-S^7 spectrum is DENSER than round-S^7
(208 vs 25 eigs in tested range). Any moderately-spaced chain gets
trivially tight median |Delta| against squashed via density-of-states
asymmetry. NOT a hidden-fiber correlation; a density artifact.

F-180-1 escalation (process-integrity):
The actual null-test code that produced p=0.041 does NOT exist in
PR #585's committed script. The p-value appears only in the NDJSON
output. Load-bearing significance claim has no auditable provenance.
Conductor decision needed.

PR #585 PRIMARY verdict (spectrally-distinct; M-theory KK spectrum
NOT bit-exactly instantiable on round-S^7) is INDEPENDENT and stands.
Only the CMB hidden-fiber sub-claim is retracted.

Recommended PR #585 amendment:
